                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "Lovely.\n\nExistential quantifiers are a standard part of predicate logic. \"Trivial\" seems a little dicier, yeah.  I assume triviality means something like it's guaranteed to always exist and be easy to find. But I'd honestly be fine with a definition where declarativity itself is a sliding scale depending on the triviality of the existential quantifier. On that basis I might still count functional programs as only slightly declarative..."
                            }
